  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "We now have three of four cells in a critical 2×2 factorial (encoder × profile): pca-single (0.485), scvi-single (0.520), and scvi-multiprofile (0.650–0.653). The missing cell is pca-multiprofile (config_002). This experiment directly tests whether the large multiprofile gain (~13 pts) is a general property of multi-profile aggregation or is specifically enabled by scvi_n200's learned latent representation. If pca-multiprofile also reaches ~0.65, the profile setting dominates and encoder choice becomes secondary; if it stays near ~0.50, the interaction between encoder and profile is the key driver, and future experiments should prioritize encoder selection. Resolving this interaction is the highest-information next step because it determines whether subsequent budget should be spent exploring new encoders (scgpt) in multiprofile, exploring multimodal fusion, or other directions. It also avoids changing multiple factors at once (only encoder differs from the best config_005, with aggregation held at avgpool where the transformer gain was negligible)."
}

